## Diff Editor: Margin and Gutter Actions

In the diff editor, the **gutter** is the narrow column that runs alongside each line of code, between the line numbers and the code itself. When you hover over the **gutter**, interactive buttons appear in it next to each block of changed lines. *- purple rectangle* 

| Action | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| **Revert Block** | An action available in the gutter next to each changed block. You can trigger it in two ways:<br><br>**Option 1 – Quick arrow:** If displayed click the arrow button that appears in the gutter directly next to the block for an instant one‑click revert.<br><br>**Option 2 – Menu:** If displayed click the `...` (ellipsis) button in the gutter and select *Revert Block* from the dropdown menu.<br><br>Both methods discard that specific block of changes, restoring those lines to their state in the older version. This lets you selectively undo individual changes without affecting other modifications in the same file. |

{{::il.Vscode_TimelineCompareButtons_img}}

